Here's an example code snippet to illustrate the test:
```java
public void testTimeout() throws TimeoutException, IOException {
    // Create a new instance of the HttpConnection class
    HttpConnection connection = null;

    // Establish a connection to a target URL
    connection = HttpConnection.connect("http://example.com", "GET");

    // Set the timeout property on the connection object
    String[] timeouts = {"10s", "5m", "1h"};
    for (String timeout : timeouts) {
        try {
            // Send an HTTP request using the established connection
            connection.post("/path/to/resource", null, null);

            // Verify that the response is received within the specified timeout period
            if (!timeout.equals("10s")) {
                throw new TimeoutException("Timeout occurred");
            }

            break;
        } catch (TimeoutException e) {
            continue;
        }
    }
}
```

